  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in sentiment (e.g., sentiment > 0.33) by 10-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward forecasts when sentiment is consistently negative (e.g., sentiment < -0.20) by adding a 5-10% bias correction to prevent premature bottoming.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates > 1.5σ from recent 7-day average, adjust toward the average by 5-10%.",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is lower than forecast by > 5% for 3 consecutive days, reduce next forecast by 5-8% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment shifts: if sentiment changes from 0.00 to 0.33 within 2 days, adjust forecast upward by 3-5% to capture momentum.",
    "Cap forecast volatility: if sentiment is neutral (0.00) and price is trending, avoid large swings; use 1-2% smoothing to prevent overfitting to noise."
  ]
}
